<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dunadd</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dunadd is a hillfort on a rocky outcrop in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilmartin">Kilmartin Glen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a>, in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. It was the main royal centre of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> from about the 6th to the 9th century, and excavations have found imported pottery, metalworking and fine jewellery. A carved footprint, basin and boar on its summit rock are thought to have been used in royal inauguration ceremonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dunadd.jpg" alt="Dunadd" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otter · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dunadd_Fort_20080427.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
